        <item>
            <title>2.2.0</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 10 Jul 2026 14:26:10 -0500</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>20260710</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.2.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <description><![CDATA[
                <h2>What's New in v2.2.0</h2>
                <h3>New</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Matchups Tab
                        <ul>
                            <li>Dedicated matchup browser that lets you browse and analyze per lane matchups.</li>
                            <li>Tracks win rate, CS/m, items and more about each matchup!</li>
                            <li>Automatically rates matchup difficulty based on rolling stats to help identify what you personally struggle with.</li>
                            <li>Quickly review kills and deaths in this matchup, break them down by in game time or review them all at once. </li>
                            <li>Quick links to popular online resources to review what other players in this matchup are doing.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Enhancements</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Notes
                        <ul>
                            <li>Notes are now broken down into Matchup Notes and Game Notes.</li>
                            <li>Added support for different fonts, sizes, and ordered lists.</li>
                            <li>Added a button to pop out the notes for either, or both, to their own floating window to allow editing notes while also playing back a recording.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li>Dashboard
                        <ul>
                            <li>New Tough Matchups and reworked Struggling Against panel.</li>
                            <li>Tough Matchups show matchups with negative win rates within the time range selected.</li>
                            <li>Struggling VS is now more generic and shows champions you're losing against in general.</li>
                            <li>Added an option to exclude support games from CS/m calculations for players who only play support occasionally or when filled.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Bugfixes</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Fixed bug that caused Chroma's to render a champions base splash on the dashboard and in posters.
                        <ul>
                            <li>Please submit bug reports if you find any Chroma's that still do not work. </li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li>Fixed a transparency bug in light and dark modes.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Quality of Life</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Matchups that an outcome is not detected, usually caused by closing the game client before Firefly captures the result from the API, will now show a question mark in your recordings. Click the question mark to mark a game as a win or loss for more accurate matchup data.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>For the full detailed changelog please visit <a href="https://fireflymac.gg/changelog.html">https://fireflymac.gg/changelog.html</a>.</p>
            ]]></description>
